      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] \nSince this platform uses the Zephyr flash page layout (as noted in the commit description), the write and erase block sizes are likely already defined in the Zephyr device tree.\n\nConsider reusing those properties via `DT_PROP` instead of hardcoding `1` and `0x1000`. This ensures a single source of truth and matches the pattern used by other chips (e.g., `rtk/include/flash_chip.h` and `stm32/include/flash_chip.h`):\n\n```c\n/* Minimum write size */\n#define CONFIG_FLASH_WRITE_SIZE \\\n\tDT_PROP(DT_INST(0, soc_nv_flash), write_block_size)\n/* Erase sector size */\n#define CONFIG_FLASH_ERASE_SIZE \\\n\tDT_PROP(DT_INST(0, soc_nv_flash), erase_block_size)\n```\n\n[🔗](http://go/tj/6e0cad92-ef62-44b0-ab27-a7edb3de84e9)",
